    "field": "Marine global change biology",
    "problem": "Experimental research on ocean change has largely focused on warming and acidification, while comparatively neglecting oxygen loss, which prevents a robust comparison of the biological threats posed by these three co-occurring stressors and potentially misdirects research and mitigation efforts.",
    "method": "This study uses sequential hierarchical mixed-model meta-analyses on 721 control-treatment comparisons from existing literature to quantitatively compare the biological impacts of current hypoxic events with those experimentally projected for future ocean warming and acidification.",
    "task": "This paper's task is to compare the biological impacts of current hypoxic events with those of future ocean warming and acidification on marine life using a hierarchical mixed-model meta-analysis of 721 experimental control-treatment comparisons from published literature.",
